  _citation_special_details
         primary   'Certification of Standard Reference Material 660c for powder diffraction'     'Pow. Dif. J.'     2020     10.1017/S0885715620000068    
; Primary paper on this SRM, 
  describing data collection and analysis using Fundamental Parameters Approach
  and Bruker AXS Topas software.

Attached measured data are exactly the raw data sets used for certification. 

However, the fits have been recomputed for the purposes of this data release. 
The instrument parameters have been re-refined, and
the calculated results field contain a pattern calculated from these new parameters.

Note: Certain commercial equipment, instruments, software, or materials are identified in this file in order to specify the experimental procedure adequately. Such identification is not intended to imply recommendation or endorsement by the U.S. government, nor is it intended to imply that the materials or equipment identified are necessarily the best available for the purpose.

;        
         machine   
; The Optics and Alignment of the Divergent Beam Laboratory 
  X-ray Powder Diffractometer and its Calibration 
  Using NIST Standard Reference Materials
;        'J. Res. NIST'      2015      10.6028/jres.120.013          'Primary description of the use of the NIST DBD' 
         machine_second_source         
;  The optics and alignment of the divergent-beam laboratory X-ray powder diffractometer 
   and its calibration using NIST standard reference materials
;        'Intl. Tables for Cryst. Vol. H, Chapter 3.1'     2019      10.1107/97809553602060000115 'Alternative source for the description of the use of the NIST DBD'  
         std_err_calc        
; Poisson errors and adaptive rebinning in 
  X-ray powder diffraction data
;        'Pow. Diff.'        2018      10.1017/S0885715618000726     
; Description of how the statistical weights are properly calculated in the data sets.
  In particular, note that the statistical weight 1/sigma^2 is tau^2/(N+1),
  where tau is the counting time, and N is the number of counts.
;        
         monochromators      
; The optics of focusing bent-crystal monochromators 
  on X-ray powder diffractometers
     with application to lattice parameter determination 
     and microstructure analysis
;        'J. Appl. Cryst.'   2019      10.1107/S1600576719010951     
; A variant of this method is used to correct the native Cu K\a spectrum for the 
  narrowing effects of the graphite monochromator.  In these files,
  the passband is taken to be Gaussian, with a width assumed to be roughly the mosaic angle, and an offset.
  There is not an extra dispersion 
  term due to the monochromator, since it is adjacent to the detector.
; 
